feat(api): recognise Kinescope video links

The API knows YouTube, Vimeo and Loom only. A Kinescope link (kinescope.io)
cannot be stored as an external video activity, the AI tools and MCP reject it
for create_media_activity and build_course, the `embed` fence and LMS import
leave it a generic iframe.

Bring back the Kinescope support that landed with learnhouse/learnhouse#1352
and was dropped again in ec9ebed5a ("chore: drop unused video embed provider"):
"kinescope" in ExternalVideoType, kinescope_id() and the embed provider in
embeds.py, kind="kinescope" for the AI tools, Kinescope iframes in
html_to_tiptap, the MCP instructions and the SDK schema (packages/sdk,
regenerated). Kinescope is stored like the other services; the web plays it
through a registered video provider. The migration docs list every external
type, Loom included.

Covered by `test_core_html_to_tiptap.py`, `test_block_specs.py`,
`test_courses.py` and `test_video_activity_updates.py`.
